  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "An Externally Owned Account (EOA) is a type of Ethereum account controlled by a private key held outside the blockchain \u2014 typically by an end user via a wallet \u2014 as opposed to a contract account controlled by smart contract code. EOAs can initiate transactions, sign messages, and hold ether and tokens; they have no associated code. Every Ethereum transaction must originate from an EOA, making them the fundamental actor type in the Ethereum account model.",
